speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, under the provisions of Standing Order 43, I ask the unanimous consent of the House to move a motion of urgent and pressing necessity.
In the light of the fact that we are going through a critical period due to inflation that reduces constantly the true purchasing power of Canadians;
That this serious situation should not allow financiers to take unfair advantage of underprivileged Canadians and that the lending institutions called "finance companies" make the most of the economic crisis at this time by using misleading advertising, trying to make people believe they will be able to solve their problems by borrowing money at high interest rates;
Seconded by the hon. member for Champlain (Mr. Matte) I move:
That the House consider as soon as possible the possibility of abolishing all advertising by finance companies so that they can no longer entice Canadians to borrow beyond their means through misleading solicitation.
